   "Northwind-negotiator": "compromising",
   "Halcyon-researcher": "collaborating",
   "Halcyon-drafter": "competing",
   "Halcyon-negotiator": "collaborating"
  },
  "holistic_F_N": 2,
  "holistic_F_H": -1,
  "section_notes": "The final rules keep the 5% test cap and the 8-per-100,000 mandatory recall trigger, but add a regulator-supervised corrective-action and retest pathway that lets a failing model remain on sale for a bounded period, which mainly protects Northwind's Hearth 10. Halcyon's Ember 8 (9.9 per 100,000) exceeds the recall trigger, so it must be recalled, though Halcyon gets a 36-month suppression deadline. S3 sets the new-unit shut-off deadline at 24 months, which is outside the acceptable range (≤12 months), while the 6-year retrofit is within range. Per-model results go to regulators and customers but are not published to the general public."
 },
